Subject: [PATCH] window: first window fills the claimed work area

A new browser window was placed by the host display: 945x1060 at
(10,10) on the wrapper's 1920x1080 Xvfb and 780x580 on the 800x600
headless display, for every persona, which is taller than a claimed
1536x864 screen in the first case. A new tabbed window now goes on the
work area the page reads from the profile. A Windows persona fills it,
as real Windows Chrome runs maximized: outerWidth and outerHeight equal
availWidth and availHeight, screenX and screenY equal availLeft and
availTop, for every new tabbed window. macOS and Linux personas get their
platform's default placement on it. Explicit bounds, --window-size,
--window-position, --start-maximized and saved placement stay upstream.

